# Furious Forebear: "Whenever a creature you control dies while this card is in your graveyard" - ruling: if the Forebear dies at the
# same time as one or more creatures you control, its ability won't trigger, for it was not in the graveyard when they died. Bot2's
# Devilthorn Fox (3/1) attacks on turn 4 and Bot1 blocks it with the Forebear (3/1) and a Memnite: the Fox deals 1 to each and all
# three die at once. Bot1 has {1}{W} available (the Plains and Mox Jet), but nothing triggers (`? Stack.Count = 0` at Bot1's
# priority in the combat damage step) and the payment is never asked (`! Bot1.Decline`) and the Forebear stays in the graveyard.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Pearl
Mox Ruby
Mox Jet
Furious Forebear
Memnite
Plains
Plains
Plains x20

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Pearl
Mox Jet
Devilthorn Fox
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Furious Forebear.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Memnite.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Devilthorn Fox.Cast
[T4 Bot2.DeclareAttackers]
Bot2.Attack(Devilthorn Fox > Bot1)
[T4 Bot2.DeclareBlockers]
Bot1.Block(Furious Forebear > Devilthorn Fox; Memnite > Devilthorn Fox)
[T4 Bot2.CombatDamage]
Bot2.Pass
? Stack.Count = 0
Bot1.Pass
! Bot1.Decline
[T4 Bot2.Main2]

[Expect]
Stack.Count = 0
Bot1.Graveyard = Memnite; Furious Forebear
Bot1.Hand = Plains; Plains
Bot2.Graveyard = Devilthorn Fox
